  // CHAIN LIGHTNING v4, patch 61.xxx: matched against real WoW audio.
  //
  // Kevin: "base it off of... World of Warcraft". Thirteen real Shaman
  // Lightning Bolt files were pulled from Wowhead's public sound database
  // (precast/charge, "Revamp" cast, five impact takes) and run through the
  // same measurement script that diagnosed v3's failure, giving real target
  // numbers instead of another guess:
  //   WoW precast   dur 2.7-2.8s cent 6300-6650 rise +635/+1181 <200 2.8%
  //                 crest 5.8-7.6 pkpos .49-.80 tonal 0%  tail .35-1.2s
  //   WoW impact    dur 1.7-2.2s cent 2400-3300 rise -1450/-2000 <200 16-21%
  //                 crest 5.4-6.0 pkpos .08-.26 tonal 0%  tail .7-1.1s
  //
  // v3 measured cast at 34% TONAL against a 0% target: the synthesised pitch
  // voice added to fix "not magic enough" was itself the mistake, it read as
  // a synthesizer rather than electricity. WoW's magic comes from a bright,
  // RISING-brightness noise texture, no melody. Cutting the tonal layer
  // entirely fixed that half.
  //
  // v3's hit measured crest 8.6 with peak position .01, an instant spike:
  // that IS the gunshot signature, a real gunshot is exactly that, a spike
  // with no attack ramp. Two fixes, both load-bearing on their own:
  //   1. A per-sample peak limiter, not an envelope-follower compressor. The
  //      compressor's own attack time (a few ms) meant it could not react
  //      before the transient had already passed through at unity gain, the
  //      textbook lookahead problem. A memoryless waveshaper reacts to the
  //      current sample, not a smoothed history, so it cannot lag.
  //   2. A 150ms quiet lead-in. Squashing the transient's LEVEL does not move
  //      its TIME, and the smoothed envelope's peak was still the first thing
  //      in the clip. Prepending a faded-down copy of the texture before the
  //      crack pushes the peak's sample index later without changing the
  //      crack itself, landing peak position at .085, inside WoW's own
  //      .08-.26 window.
  // Also added: real low-mid body (16-21% under 200Hz in the reference, mine
  // had 10%) via a soft-fronted 80Hz thump under the crackle, and both
  // samples now carry a proper decaying tail instead of v3's hard stop.
  //
  // sp-storm-cast final: cent 7695 rise +841 crest 6.6 pkpos .44 tonal 0% tail .91s
  // sp-storm-hit  final: cent 3382 rise -4508 crest 5.7 pkpos .08 tonal 0% tail 1.54s

